          "rdfs:Class",
          "schema:Thing"
        ],
        "@id": "prototype:bf34c4e2-7f7e-4332-a074-97aa851b8c9c",
        "rdfs:label": "API Connection",
        "rdfs:comment": "An application programming interface (API) is a connection between computers or between computer programs. It is a type of software interface, offering a service to other pieces of software. A document or standard that describes how to build such a connection or interface is called an API specification. A computer system that meets this standard is said to implement or expose an API. The term API may refer either to the specification or to the implementation.",
        "name": "API Connection",
        "description": "An application programming interface (API) is a connection between computers or between computer programs. It is a type of software interface, offering a service to other pieces of software. A document or standard that describes how to build such a connection or interface is called an API specification. A computer system that meets this standard is said to implement or expose an API. The term API may refer either to the specification or to the implementation.",
        "rdfs:seeAlso": [
          "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/API"
        ],
        "rdfs:isDefinedBy": {
